API-02: a lifecycle call in the wrong state no longer puts the engine in ERROR_STATE

SWMMEngine refuses open/initialize/start/step/end/report in the wrong state
with SWMM_ERR_LIFECYCLE through set_error(), which also set the state to
ERROR_STATE. A refused swmm_engine_step before swmm_engine_start then made
start fail, and a refused call during a run made the next step fail. Keep
the error code and message, but leave the state unchanged for this code.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-02_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..449da95 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -7988,7 +7988,9 @@ void SWMMEngine::write_open_failure_report() noexcept {
 void SWMMEngine::set_error(int code, const char* message) noexcept {
     ctx_.error_code    = code;
     ctx_.error_message = message ? message : "";
-    ctx_.state         = EngineState::ERROR_STATE;
+    // A call made in the wrong state is refused; it must not end the run.
+    if (code != SWMM_ERR_WRONG_STATE)
+        ctx_.state     = EngineState::ERROR_STATE;
     emit_warning(code, message);
 }
 
